WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:10.440
In summer 2018, Arne Duncan published a
memoir. After presiding over nearly a

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.880
decade of academic stagnation and the
failure of high-profile initiatives,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.600
there are many lessons he might have
shared. Instead, he seems to have learned

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.080
little while in office.
Here are three things Duncan never

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.060
learned, but which reformers should take
to heart. One: It's hard to persuade

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:32.250
people you disdain. Duncan shrugged off
anxieties about the Common Core is the

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.780
product of moms who fear "their child isn't as brilliant as they thought they

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.550
were." Two: It's tempting to ignore
inconvenient realities. Many parents

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.329
thought tests were more focused on
measuring schools than on helping their

00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:50.489
kids. They had a point! But Duncan
dismisses such concerns. Three: It's easy to

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:55.020
blame bad messaging for policy failures.
Duncan has trouble thinking of anything

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.399
he'd have done differently, insisting
that any setbacks were the product of poor

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:03.809
PR. The disappointments of Duncan's
tenure have valuable lessons to teach —

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:06.740
but only if we're willing to learn them.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.080
What lessons do you think school

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.700
reformers need to learn? Let us know in
your comments. Also, let us know what

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:18.689
other topics you'd like our scholars to
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:24.049
and subscribe for more research and
videos from AEI.

